1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Thaumastus''' (c400-after 469), an uncle of [http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Sidonius-Apollinarius-Bishop-of-Clermont/6000000009437556787 Sidonius], and son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Apollinaris-III-Praeto
2 CONC rian-Prefect-of-Gaul/6000000000312655223 Apollinaris]. See Christian Settipani, [http://francia.digitale-sammlungen.de/Blatt_bsb00016294,00213.html?prozent=1 Ruricius Ier évêque de Limoges et ses relations familiales] in ''Francia
2 CONC '' 18/1 (1991), 203.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thaumastus I (also called Thaumaste I) (born c. 400)[1] was a friend and uncle of Sidonius Apollinaris. His brother, the elder Apollinaris was born around 405[2] and was the Prefect of Gaul under Valentinian III between 425 and 45
2 CONC 5.[3] Thaumastus and his brother were both sons of another Apollinaris, Praetorian Prefect of Gaul before 409[4] and were friends with his successor Decimus Rusticus. Thaumastus was associated with Tonantius Ferreolus in the impea
2 CONC chment of Arvandus[5]. He was the father of Eulalia, born in 425[2] and married before 450 to Flavius Probus, Roman Senator.
2 CONT
2 CONT He seems to be a descendant of another Apollinaris, Prefect of Gaul under Constantine II between 337 and 340.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References and citations
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genea
2 CONC logica, 2002)
2 CONT    2. ^ a b Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989)
2 CONT    3. ^ a b Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et G
2 CONC enealogica, 2002)
2 CONT    4. ^ Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genea
2 CONC logica, 2002)</
2 CONT    5. ^ Sidonius Apollinaris, The Letters of Sidonius (Oxford: Clarendon, 1915), pp. clx-clxxxiii
2 CONT
