2 CONT 5.   MUNDERIC of vitry-en-Parthois, very young when his father was murdered 509; revolted 532 against a son of CLOVIS [I] the Great, King Theodoric of Austrasia, who lured him from his fortress by a pledge of safe conduct. Instead
2 CONC  MUNDERIC was beset and killed "but left a pile of enemies around his corpse."  He mar. ARTHEMIA.
