1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Chlothar I "the Old" de Soissons, King of the Franks=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Clovis I the Great, King of the Franks and Chlotilde of Burgundy 
2 CONT *[https://www.facebook.com/Merovingians-The-Once-The-Present-Future-kings-471707109534948/ Facebook Merovingians: The Once, The Present,  & Future kings]
2 CONT * not the father of https://www.geni.com/people/Blithilde-false-historian-daughter-of-Clothar-I/6000000090668222127
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Clovis-I-the-Great-King-of-the-Franks/6000000005913350166?through=6000000005913253971 CHLODOVECH] [Clovis] ([464/67]-Paris [27 Nov] 511, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-
2 CONC Geneviève]). m [secondly] (492) [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlotilde-of-Burgundy/6000000001947211337 CHROTECHILDIS] [Clotilde/Rotilde[48]] of Burgundy, daughter of CHILPERICH King of Burgundy & his wife --- ([480]-Tours, monaste
2 CONC ry of Saint-Martin 544 or 548, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]).  King Clovis & his second wife had [six] children:[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS] & h
2 CONC ttp://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDY%20KINGS.htm#ChrotechildisOrClotildedied544
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Ingomer/6000000003098272663?through=6000000005913350166 INGOMER] (b and d 493). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>3.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodomir-I-King-the-Franks-at-Orl%C3%A9ans/6000000010395927288?through=6000000005913350166 CHLODOMER] ([494/95]-killed in battle Vézeronce 21 Jun 524).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>4.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Child%C3%A9bert-I-King-of-the-Franks-at-Paris/6000000007815238292?through=6000000005913350166 CHILDEBERT] ([497]-23 Dec 558, bur Paris, Saint-Germain des Prés). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>5.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlothar-I-the-Old-King-of-the-Franks/5585928797380086234?through=6000000005913350166 '''CHLOTHACHAR'''] [Clotaire/Lothar] ([501/02]-Soissons [30 Nov/31 Dec] 561, bur Soissons, basilique 
2 CONC Saint-Médard).   Gregory of Tours names Clotaire as son of King Clovis and his wife Clotilde, listed after Childebert[145].  "Theodorico, Chlomiro, Hildeberto, Hlodario" are named (in order) as sons of "Chlodoveus" in the Regum Me
2 CONC rowingorum Genealogia[146].  He succeeded his father in 511 as CLOTAIRE I King of the Franks, at Soissons, his territory covering Soissons, Laon, Noyon, Arras, Cambrai, Tournai and the lower Meuse, the lands which were later to be
2 CONC come the kingdom of Neustria.  Gregory of Tours records that King Clotaire and his half-brother King Theoderich invaded Thuringia in 531, deposed King Hermanfred and annexed the kingdom, specifying that Clotaire brought his second
2 CONC  wife back as part of his booty[147].  He and his brother King Childebert launched a third attack on Burgundy, besieged Autun and occupied the whole kingdom, deposing King Gondemar II[148] in 534.  He invaded Spain, with his broth
2 CONC er King Childebert, and besieged Zaragoza but was forced to withdraw[149].  He inherited the territories of his great-nephew King Theodebert in 555 and those of his brother King Childebert in 558, when he became sole king of the F
