2 CONT Page 66:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.   CHLOTAIRE I, 499-561.  Upon the death of CLOVIS the kingdom was divided among his four sons, but as each died a redistribution took place until CHLOTAIRE, the youngest had it all in 558.  His realm extended from the Rhinme to
2 CONC  the Channel and southward into Aquitaine.  He mar. (1) St. REDEGONDE, dau of a Thuringian Frankish king whom he had deteated in battle, taking the princess as booty.  Soon after their marriage, she founded a convent at Poitiers w
2 CONC here she became a nun in 554 and where she died.  When CHLOTAIRE d., the kingdom again was divided among four sons.
2 CONT
