2 CONT Source: "The Franks" by Edward James.   Franks: Had unknown first wife, then Fredegund, who was set aside so he could marry Galswinth (Brunhild's sister). Shortly after the marriage, the couple quarrelled over Fredegund and Galswi
2 CONC nth was found strangled in bed. Chilperic then married Fredegund again.   Chilperic was assassinated in 584 while hunting at Chelles, near Paris. As Chilperic was dismounting from his horse, a man stepped forward and stabbed him.
2 CONT    Other sources: RC 303; AF; "Women in the Wall" chart.
2 CONT    RC: Chilperic I of Soissons, 561.   "Women in the Wall" chart says the first wife was Audovera.
2 CONT    Wall: Chilperic of Neustria, died 584.
