1 NOTE the second wife of the Roman Emperor Valentinian I (reigned 364-375) and the mother of Valentinian II (reigned 375-392), Galla and Justa.
2 CONT She was born into a family of senatorial rank in Sicily, she was at first the wife of the usurper Magnentius (d. 353). Valentinian divorced his first wife on her account and married her not later than 370. She thus became the step
2 CONC mother of the future emperor Gratian. During the reign of Gratian she lived in Sirmium, but during the reign of her son, who succeeded as a child, was effective ruler in his stead and lived with him in Milan.
2 CONT For years she fought Saint Ambrose in the conflict over Arianism, but was at last defeated. In 388 she fled with her son to Theodosius in Thessaloniki Greece, before the invasion of Italy by the usurper Maximus, and seems to have 
2 CONC died shortly afterwards.
