2 CONT Notes from  https://www.geni.com/people/Sharon-Richards/6000000018964631151 user: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''<<Menia herself married a second time to '''an unknown by name member of the noble Lombard family of Gauss'''; >>. ''
2 CONT I don't know if it is the translation or just ingnorance but this is completely wrong.  The Gaussi became an important ruling clan of the Lombards in the late 6th century...probably after Audoin's son, Alboin  led them into Italy:
2 CONT
2 CONT  - - - - - - - - - - -
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Pitzia was a valuable military asset of King Theodoric I -Ostrogothic King of Italy.  He served in many battles in Pannonia and the hinterlands of the Eastern Empire.  As a Gausi, or Geat, he was a Goth by birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Menia and they had Audoin.  Interestingly, Amalaberga, the wife of Hermenfried was the daughter of Amalafrida and Thrasamond of the Vandals; Amalafrida was the daughter of Theodomir and the sister  of Theodoric "the gre
2 CONC at" Ostrogoth king of Italy, making Amalaberga his niece. Given these connections it is highly likely that Count Pitzia knew the family and would have been accepted as the second husband of Menia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately late in the career of Theodoric "the great", he murdered Count Pitzia over some dispute involving perceived  disloyalty and it is said that he lived to regret his actions.- Wolfram, Herwig, "The History of the Goths"
2 CONT
2 CONT  - - - - - - - - -  -
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gausi traced their lineage back to the Goths and they were a prominent family when, in 539, the tribe came under the rule of a minor, Walthari of the Lethings clan, and a Gausian, Audoin, was elected his regent. In 547, Audoin
2 CONC  succeeded Walthari, who died young of natural causes, and assumed the royal mantle by usurpation. Audoin's son and successor, Alboin, led the Lombards into Italy in 569 and died without male heirs in 572 or 573. He had made the L
2 CONC ombard kings into kings of Italy. His successor was Cleph of the Beleos clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Gausian_dynasty
2 CONT
