2 CONT
2 CONT     * James, Edward (1991). The Franks. London: Blackwell, ISBN 0 63114 872 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Oman, Charles (1914). The Dark Ages, 476–918. London: Rivingtons.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Wallace-Hadrill, J. M. (1962). The Long-Haired Kings, and Other Studies in Frankish History. London: Methuen.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Wood, Ian N. (1994). The Merovingian Kingdoms, 450–751. London: Longman, ISBN 0 58221 878 0.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Depiction: A treaty of King Chlothar II and the Lombards.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar II (or Chlotar, Clothar, Clotaire, Chlotochar, or Hlothar, giving rise to Lothair; 584 – 629), called the Great (le Grand) or the Young (le Jeune), King of Neustria, and, from 613 to 629, King of all the Franks, was not y
2 CONC et born when his father, King Chilperic I died in 584. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother, Fredegund, was regent until her death in 597, at which time the thirteen-year-old Chlothar began to rule for himself. As king, he continued his mother's feud with Brunhilda, queen of Austrasia, with equal viciousness a
2 CONC nd bloodshed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first wife of Chlothar II was Haldetrude (ca 575–604). She was the mother of Dagobert I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chlothar's second wife was Bertrada. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His third wife was Sichilde, who bore him Charibert II and a daughter, Oda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Bachrach, Bernard S. (1972). Merovingian Military Organization, 481–751. Minneapolis: University of Minnesota Press, ISBN 0 81660 621 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Geary, Patrick J. (1988). Before France and Germany: The Creation and Transformation of the Merovingian World. Oxford: Oxford University Press, ISBN 0 19504 458 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT * James, Edward (1991). The Franks. London: Blackwell, ISBN 0 63114 872 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Oman, Charles (1914). The Dark Ages, 476–918. London: Rivingtons.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wallace-Hadrill, J. M. (1962). The Long-Haired Kings, and Other Studies in Frankish History. London: Methuen.
2 CONT
