1 NOTE Childebert I
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=4bfd2b01-b5ae-484d-9c0d-a92348fea3c3&tid=6650027&pid=-1179323971
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-7369
1 NOTE KING OF PARIS 511
1 NOTE [FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT    Merovingian king of Paris from 511, who helped to incorporate Burgundyinto the Frankish realm.
2 CONT    Childebert was a son of Clovis I and Clotilda. He received lands innorthwestern France,
2 CONT stretching from the Somme down to Brittany, in the partition of hisfather's kingdom in 511; to these he added part of the kingdom of Orléansin the 520s (by the murder of his brother Chlodomer's young heirs), partof the kingdom of 
2 CONC Burgundy in 534 (by conquest, with his brother ChlotarI), and Provence in 537 (by treaty). After a campaign in 531against theVisigoths, who still held the coastal strip between the Rhône and thePyrenees, he invaded Spain itself in
2 CONC  542 in alliance with Chlotar;although the expedition had no great success, he did bring back with himthe tunic of the martyred St. Vincent, housing this in a new foundationat Paris that came to be called Saint-Germain-des-Prés. C
2 CONC hildebert leftno sons, and his lands were taken over by Chlotar on his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT To cite this page: "Childebert I" Encyclopædia Britannica
2 CONT  <http://www.britannica.com/eb/article?idxref=464438>
