1 NOTE 1  NAME Cloderic I (Childeric) of the /Franks/ 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001 1  NAME Chirderic I /Meroving/ 1  BIRT 2  DATE ABT. 436 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001 1  DE
2 CONC AT 2  DATE 481 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: RC 303; Kraentzler 1657, 1777, 1780; AF; "The Franks" by Edward James; Pfafman.   Franks: The grave of Cloderic/Childeric I was found in 1653 in Tournai, Belgium. It contained "gold-and-garnet belt and equipment fittings;
2 CONC  gold buckles and a gold arm-ring; a brooch of the type worn on the right shoulder by high Roman officials; a Frankish throwing-axe, or francisca; the fittings for a sword or scramasax (a single-edged sword); the famous gold bees 
2 CONC which Napoleon took to be a symbol of French royalty, and which led him to wear a cloak bejewelled with such bees at his imperial coronation...There were also coins in the grave, and, finally, the crucial find, Childeric's seal-ri
2 CONC ng, with the inscription CHILDERICI REGIS ('belonging to King Childeric'), and its portrayal of the long-haired king wearing Roman-style military dress and bearing a lance."   RC: Cloderic I, King of Franks, 458-481. Married about
2 CONC  465.   K: Childeric/Childerich I, King of Franks/King of a part of Salistian Franks. Married 463, died 481.
2 CONT    Pfafman: Childeric I, King of Salic Franks 458-481.
