2 CONT * THEODERICH ([485]-end 533, bur Metz).  Gregory of Tours names Theoderich as son of King Clovis by one of his mistresses, born before his marriage to Clotilde[55].  "Theodorico, Chlomiro, Hildeberto, Hlodario" are named (in order
2 CONC ) as sons of "Chlodoveus" in the Regum Merowingorum Genealogia
2 CONT * Theuderic I[a] (c. 485 – 533/4) was the Merovingian king of Metz, Rheims, or Austrasia—as it is variously called—from 511 to 533 or 534.
