2 CONT Merwig II, King of Thuringia, from about 408 to 451
2 CONT
2 CONT King Merwig II. was killed in Chalons in 451
2 CONT
2 CONT The Battle of Châlons or the Battle of the Catalaunian Plains took place on June 20, 451 between the Roman forces, composed mostly of foederati (Germanic Barbarian mercenary soldiers) led by the Roman General Flavius Aëtius and th
2 CONC e king of the Visigoths, Theodoric I, against the Huns and their vassals led by the king of the Huns, Attila. This battle was the last significant military operation of the West Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT The rest of the Thuringian army settled between Meuse and Schelde in today's Belgium, which led to a significant decline in the population of Thuringia, why they did this is unclear today.
2 CONT
