2 CONC "[33].  The Chronicle of Marcellinus also records that "Placidia Honorii principis sorore" was abducted by "Halaricus" and later married "Athaulfo propinquo suo"[34].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Captured by Alaric King of the Visigoths during the sack of Rome in Aug 409, she passed to Ataulf on his accession as king[35].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicon of Bishop Idatius records that “Ataulfus” married “Placidiam” at Narbonne in 414[36].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first husband married her after failing to establish an alliance with Emperor Honorius[37].  
