2 CONT As part of the peace negotiated by King Walia with the Romans in 416, Galla Placidia was returned to her brother Honorius in early 416[38].  The Chronicon Albeldense names “Ballia” as successor of “Sigericus”, adding that he made 
2 CONC peace with Emperor Honorius and returned his sister Placidia to him[39].  
