1 NOTE Constantius III (died 421), Western Roman emperor (421). A general in the 
2 CONT service of the Western emperor Honorius (384-423), Constantius became 
2 CONT virtual ruler of the western provinces in 414, when he forced the 
2 CONT Visigoths out of Gaul into Spain. In 417 he married Honorius's sister, 
2 CONT Galla Placidia. The next year he recalled the Visigoths from Spain and 
2 CONT established a kingdom for them in southern Gaul under their ruler Wallia 
2 CONT (reigned 415-19). During the last year of his life, Constantius was 
2 CONT officially recognized by Honorius as co-emperor.
