1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT He was proclaimed Most Noble (Nobilissimus) by his uncle Honorius before 423.
2 CONT Nobilissimus between 423 and 424. Caesar in 424. He and Licinia Eudokia
2 CONT Theodosia, augusta were engaged in 424.1 He succeeded John as Emperor of the
2 CONT West in 425. Emperor in Western Roman Empire, between 425 and 16 March 455.
2 CONT He issued, acting in conjunction with Pope Leo I the Great, the famous Novel
2 CONT 17, which assigned to the bishop of Rome supremacy over the provincial
2 CONT churches in 444.3 He was had the Roman General ’tius, who defeated Atilla the
2 CONT Hun at Chalons in 451, killed in 454. He murdered, as a result of false
2 CONT information that made him his doubt loyalty, Aetius, the great patrician, with
2 CONT his own hands in the imperial palace on 21 September 454 in Rome, Italy.
