2 CONC iæ Francorum records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[113].  In a later passage, Gregory records that the two older sons w
2 CONC ere murdered by their uncle King Clotaire, who suspected that his mother was plotting for their succession to the throne, specifying that the younger son was 7 years old[114]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#Clov
2 CONC isIB MEDLANDS]'''
