2 CONC orum records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[116].  In a later passage, Gregory records that Chlodovald escaped the fate 
2 CONC of his brothers and entered a religious life[117].  He became a monk at Nogent (now Saint-Cloud), near Paris, where he founded the monastery of Saint-Martin, renamed Saint-Cloud by the 8th century.   The Vita Sancti Chlodovaldi re
2 CONC cords the death of Chlodovald on "VII Id Sep" but does not specify the year[118].  He was canonised as St Cloud, feast day 7 Sep[119]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS]'''
