2 CONC enator of Rome
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was a Gallo-Roman Senator. He was at Rome in 469 and 475. He appears as a Vir Clarissimus (a title meaning "most eminent man") between 507 and 511. He was a friend and relative of Sidonius Apollinarus. He was vi
2 CONC sited by his cousin St. Apollinaris of Valence in 517.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
