1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liutprand_of_Benevento
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Liutprand''' (died after 759) was the duke of Benevento from the death of his father Gisulf II in 749 until his own deposition. He reigned under the regency of his mother, Scauniperga, who supported King Aistulf, until 756.
2 CONT
2 CONT After he attained his majority, he commended his duchy to Pepin the Short, King of the Franks, probably at the coaxing of Pope Stephen II, and rebelled against King Desiderius, being deposed in 758 to be replaced by [https://www.g
2 CONC eni.com/people/Arechi-II-di-Benevento/305959636230001507 Arechis II]. The Roman Emperor Constantine V offered to capture the fleeing Liutprand if Desiderius would attack the papacy until a Roman force from Sicily could join him. D
2 CONC esiderius did not attack and Liutprand was not captured.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Arechi-II-di-Benevento/305959636230001507 Arechis] was the son of '''Duke Liutprand''', whom he succeeded in 758.''[2] ''
2 CONT    [2] Kreutz 1991, p. 5. 
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arechis_II_of_Benevento
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Arechi-II-di-Benevento/305959636230001507 seems the assigned successor, not a documented son. 
2 CONT Wiki ITA, however, does not exclude kinship.
2 CONT Wiki ENG on the other hand, declares him to be his son, citing a page of studies.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN%20ITALY,%20PRE-NORMAN.htm#Arichisdied787
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Gisulf II & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''LUITPRAND''' (-after 758).  He succeeded his father as LUITPRAND Duke of Benevento.  The Chronicon Vulturnense records that "Domna Scaniperga et Domnus…Liuprand summi Ducibus gentis Langobardorum" donated serfs to Vo
2 CONC lturno monastery by charter dated Nov 747[85].  He revolted against Desiderius King of the Lombards, who deposed him in 758, replacing him as duke by Arechis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liutprando_di_Benevento cites 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sergio Rovagnati, I Longobardi, p. 115; secondo il Lexikon des Mittelalters, Liutprando fu duca dal 749 al 759.
2 CONT # Vittorio Spreti, Enciclopedia storico-nobiliare italiana pagina 179 volume B - D, Forni, 1968. URL consultato l'8 gennaio 2011.«Traevano origine da Liutprando discendente da Agisulfo I»
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lexikon des Mittelalters: Liutprand Herzog von Benevent (749-759).
2 CONT # Sergio Rovagnati, I Longobardi, Milano, Xenia, 2003, ISBN 88-7273-484-3.
2 CONT # Liutprando di Spoleto, in Dizionario biografico degli italiani, Istituto dell'Enciclopedia Italiana
2 CONT .
