1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupilia
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Rupilia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Rupilia Faustina (c. 87-bef. 138) was an influential Roman noblewoman. She was the daughter of Salonina Matidia and suffect consul Lucius Scribonius Libo Rupilius Frugi Bonus. She possibly had another sister called Rupilia Annia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother’s maternal uncle was the Roman Emperor Trajan. Her elder half-sisters were Roman Empress Vibia Sabina and Matidia Minor. The sisters lived and were raised as a part of the household of Trajan, his wife Pompeia Plotina a
2 CONC nd her father. Roman Emperor Hadrian was her brother-in-law and third cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Faustina married Marcus Annius Verus, who was a prefect in Rome and served as consul three times. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Annia Galeria Faustina or Faustina the Elder, a Roman Empress who married Roman Emperor Antoninus Pius.
2 CONT * Marcus Annius Libo, a consul.
2 CONT * Marcus Annius Verus, a praetor who married Domitia Lucilla and became father to future Roman Emperor Marcus Aurelius and his sister Annia Cornificia Faustina.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupilia
