2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titus_Flavius_Sabinus_I '''Titus Flavius Sabinus'''] (c. 20 BC - aft. 9, fl. 1st century BC to 1st century AD) was the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Titus-Flavius-Petro/6000000013205685076 Titus 
2 CONC Flavius Petro] and wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Tertulla/6000000006101312593 ... Tertulla].
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an Equestrian from Reate (modern Rieti) in the Sabine region of Italy. He served as a customs official and then as a banker in the customs in the province of Asia, where he was honoured with statues dedicated "To an Honest 
2 CONC Tax-gatherer", and later as a banker at Aventicum among the Helvetii in Gaul, where he died.
2 CONT
