2 CONT Tonantius Ferreolus, Prefect (405 or ca 420 – 475), was the Praetorian Prefect of Gaul (praefectus praetorio Galliarum) from 451. He was either "personally related to" or "connected through (...) relatives" with Sidonius Apollinar
2 CONC is,[citation needed] and was associated with Thaumastus I (?) in the impeachment of Arvandus.[citation needed] He was the son of Ferreolus, born say 390, and wife Syagria, clarissima femina (?), born say 390[citation needed] , and
2 CONC  thus maternal grandson of Flavius Afranius Syagrius, Consul in 382. He married Papianilla, clarissima femina, born ca 415, a niece of Emperor Avitus[citation needed] and the first cousin of another Papianilla, wife of Sidonius Ap
2 CONC ollinaris, and they had many children, among whom Tonantius Ferreolus.[citation needed] She was a partner who shared his troubles, according to Sidonius.
