2 CONT - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincent_of_L%C3%A9rins
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letteral/Lupis/Stirpe_Luporum.html#CAPOSTIPITE_DEI_LUPI_DI_SORAGNA_1198
2 CONT
2 CONT  B.. Saint Vincent of Lerins  (+ ca. 445 A.D.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Vincent was born in Toul in Gaul; he was the brother of Saint Lupus, Bishop of Troyes, who was a companion of Saint Germanus of Auxerre. Saint Vincent was first a soldier, then left the world to become a monk of the renowned
2 CONC  monastery of Lerins, where he was also ordained priest. He is known for his Commonitorium, which he wrote as an aid to distinguish the true teachings of the Church from the confusions of heretics; his most memorable saying is tha
2 CONC t Christians must follow that Faith which has been believed "everywhere, always, and by all." He wrote the Commonitorium about the year 434, three years dopo iler the Third Ecumenical Council in Ephesus, which he mentions in the C
2 CONC ommonitorium, and defends calling the holy Virgin Theotokos, "She who gave birth to God," in opposition to the teachings of Nestorius which were condemned at the Third Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Vincent reposed in peace about the year 445.
