1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Her name is unknown, but is reconstructed as '''Syagria''' or '''Flavia Syagria''' based on naming patterns. She is described by online sources (Wikipedia, etc.) as a "clarissima femina" who is presumed to be born 
2 CONC around the same time as her husband, [https://www.geni.com/people/Tonantius-Ferreolus/6000000007764441699 Tonantius Ferreolus]. According to the reconstruction of this pedigree by Christian Settipani, she was probably daughter of 
2 CONC [http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Afranius-Syagrius/6000000005796966019 Flavius Afranius Syagrius].
2 CONT
2 CONT From the French Wikipedia page on her son, [https://www.geni.com/people/Tonantius-Ferreolus-II/6000000007337035804 Tonantius Ferreolus]:
2 CONT
2 CONT >He was a member of the Syagrii family (maternal grandson of Consul Flavius Afranius Syagrius of 382), he was also a relative of Sidonius Apollinaris. Their wives indeed had the same name of Papianille which may suggest that they 
2 CONC were relatives (the wife of Sidonius was herself the daughter of Emperor Avitus).
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonantius_Ferreolus_(pr%C3%A9fet)
2 CONT
2 CONT In other references, the lady, holder of the profile, is also designated Clarissima Afrânius des Arvernnes (or Auvergne, Alvernia or Arvenia) in French: AuvergneA, in reference to the portion of the future French territory, and wh
2 CONC ich was at that time, ruled by her father, Flavius ​​Syagrius, in the name of Rome
