1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Erchambaldus''' ('''Erchenaud''') was Mayor of the Palaces of Neustria (641-657/8) and Burgundy (642-657/8). He was murdered 657/8, and succeeded in both offices by [http://www.geni.com/people/Ebroin/60000000057
2 CONC 47660129 Ébroïn]. He might have been a son of Ego of Alsace and Gerberge of Burgundy and Franconia, but see discussion below.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Fredegar, he was a relative of [http://www.geni.com/people/Beretrudis-of-the-Burgundians/6000000010094943325 Beretrudis], mother of [http://www.geni.com/people/Dagobert-I-King-of-the-Franks/6000000005912902306 Dagober
2 CONC t I] ("Erchynoaldus . . . consanguineus . . . de genetricis Dagoberti"). [Fredegar, Chronicle (about 660).] The exact relationship is unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Settipani suggests Beretrudis was daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Richemir-duke-of-the-Burgundians-Franconians/290459821900001444 Richomer of Burgundy] and his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Gertrude-abbess-of-Hama
2 CONC ge/290460696890002594 Garitrudis], and Erchenaud was son of Beretrudis' sister [http://www.geni.com/people/Gerberge-of-Burgundy-Franconia/6000000000437969821 Gerberge] (Settipani (1993), 95)
2 CONT
2 CONT Evans calls him a relative of Dagobert I through his mother (apparently understanding Fredegar to mean that the relationship was through Erchinoald's mother rather than through Dagobert's mother). If so, Levillain considers it lik
2 CONC ely that Erchinoald was a son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Warnacher-II-Mayor-of-the-Palaces-of-Burgundy-Austrasia/6000000000279273366 Garnier], major domus, by [http://www.geni.com/people/Bertha-of-the-Franks/600000001663246177
2 CONC 4 Berthe], daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Chlothar-II-the-Young-King-of-the-Franks/5544182020970135787 Chlothar II] by Bertetrudis.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
