1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Vitrasia Faustina=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Vitrasia Faustina (died 182 or 183) was a noble Roman woman that lived in the 2nd century during the Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vitrasia was the daughter of Annia Fundania Faustina and the Roman politician Titus Pomponius Proculus Vitrasius Pollio and her brother was Titus Fundanius Vitrasius Pollio. Her paternal grandfather was Titus Vitrasius Pollio cons
2 CONC ul of 137, while her maternal grandparents were the consul Marcus Annius Libo and Fundania. Through her maternal grandfather, she was a distant relative to the ruling Nerva–Antonine dynasty of the Roman Empire. Vitrasia was born a
2 CONC nd raised in Rome.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vitrasia through inheritances became a very wealthy heiress and had moved to Cales. Due to her influence, status and connections, Vitrasia became a public benefactor and a prominent citizen of Cales. Through her wealth, Vitrasia p
2 CONC aid for the construction or repair for the Magna Dea Temple or Temple of the Great Mother in the city.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is uncertain if Vitrasia had ever married or had children. It 182 or 183, she was involved in one of numerous conspiracies against her unstable maternal second cousin the Roman Emperor Commodus who ruled 180-192. She was execut
2 CONC ed on the orders of Commodus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitrasia_Faustina
