1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Julianus
2 CONT
2 CONT Julius Julianus (fl. 315–325) was a politician of the Roman Empire, related to the Constantinian dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Life ===
2 CONT
2 CONT He served Licinius as praetorian prefect from at least spring 315 to September 324, until Constantine I definitively defeated Licinius. However, the fall of Licinius did not mark the end of Julianus' career, as Constantine had pra
2 CONC ised Julianus' administration of the State[1] and choose him, in 325, to replace a consul fallen in disgrace, Valerius Proculus.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was probably the father of Basilina, wife of Constantine's half brother Julius Constantius and mother of emperor Julian; he was probably related to Eusebius of Caesarea.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Notes ===
2 CONT
2 CONT # Libanius, Orations 18.9
2 CONT
2 CONT === Bibliography ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Timothy David Barnes, Constantine and Eusebius, Harvard University Press, 1981, ISBN 0674165314, pp. 70, 214.
2 CONT * Robert Browning, The Emperor Julian, University of California Press, 1978, ISBN 0520037316, p. 32.
