2 CONT Flavius Liberalis From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Flavius Liberalis was a Roman of the 1st century and was a man of equestrian rank, who came from Ferentium (modern Ferento) a country town in Italy. This man of humble origin
2 CONC s was a quaestor and later a law clerk. Liberalis had his daughter Flavia Domitilla appear before a board of arbitration to prove her claim for Roman Citizenship, instead of a Latin one. She later married the future Emperor Vespas
2 CONC ian. Her children with Vespasian were Domitilla the Younger and Emperors Titus and Domitian.
