2 CONT
2 CONT [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grimoald_III_de_Bénévent '''Grimoald III'''] of Benevento, born after the year 758, was unduc and Lombard prince of Benevento from May 788 to his death in November/December 806.  He married a certain
2 CONC  '''Euanthia''' around 789/791 whom he repudiated in 795.
2 CONT
2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN%20ITALY,%20PRE-NORMAN.htm#Arichisdied787
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT  Duke Arichis & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''b. ''GRIMOALD'' (-Apr 806, bur Salerno Cathedral).  "Rumoldum et Grimoldum" are named as sons of "Aragisus" by Einhard[116].  The Chronicon Salernitanum names (in order) "Romoald, Grimoald et Gisifum, Theoderadam et Adelchisam" 
2 CONC as children of Duke Arichis and Adalperga[117].  …].  The Annales Beneventani record the death of Prince Grimoald in 806[130].  The Chronicon Salernitanum records that "Grimoald" was buried "in…ecclesia sedis Salernitanæ iuxta sep
2 CONC ulchra patris fratrisque"[131].  The Epitaphium Grimoaldi records that "vixisti septem [ter binis floridus annis]"[132].  ''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [789/91], repudiated [795] ) '''EUANTHIA''', daughter of --- & his wife Hypatia.  Erchempert records that "Grimoalt neptem augusti Achivorum in coniugium sumpsit nomine Wautiam"[133].  The Vita Philareti by Niketas of Am
2 CONC nia records the marriage of Euanthia, granddaughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Philaretos-of-Phaplagonien/4039830539610027513 Philaretos] (and sister of Maria, first wife of [https://www.geni.com/people/Konstantinos-VI-
2 CONC Porphyrog%C3%A9nete-Byzantine-Emperor/6000000000417201595 Emperor Konstantinos VI]), to "un roi des Lombards nommé Argousis"[134].  Her repudiation is referred to in a letter from Theodore the Studite to Emperor Konstantinos VI re
2 CONC proaching him of his licentious lifestyle alleging that it provoked "la répudiation d´une épouse légitime dans une contrée lointaine"[135].  The dating of the repudiation is presumably around the same time as Emperor Konstantinos 
2 CONC repudiated his first wife [dated to Jan 895], which is recorded by Theophanes[136]. 
