1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''She was probably the daughter of a certain Munatius, who was the Comes of Tiberius at his diplomatic mission in the East. In this case she was the granddaughter of Lucius Munatius Plancus, who had been consul in 
2 CONC 42 BC''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Munatia Plancina''' (died 33 AD) was a Roman noblewoman who lived in the early times of the Empire founded by Augustus. She was the wife of the governor of Syria, Gnaeus Calpurnius Piso. The couple was accused of poisoning Germ
2 CONC anicus, the nephew and adopted son of the Emperor Tiberius. At first Munatia Plancina was acquitted but when the trial was renewed she committed suicide.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Munatia_Plancina
2 CONT
