2 CONT which Wagner, Sir Anthony Richard; ‘Pedigree and Progress: Essays in the Genealogical Interpretation of History’ – says resulted in the birth of a daughter: Berenike of Commagene (b after 50), I can find the following '''contradic
2 CONC tory''' sources on the net: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *>“Epiphanes was betrothed in 43/44 to the princess Drusilla, who was a daughter of Judean King Agrippa I. Agrippa thought that Epiphanes would embrace the religion Judaism and Jewish customs. However, Epiphanes never married Drus
2 CONC illa because he refused to adopt the customs and religion of the Jews. The marriage between Epiphanes and Drusilla had not been contracted on the death of Agrippa I. '''Later Epiphanes was  betrothed to Drusilla’s sister Mariamne.
2 CONC  In 49/50, the brother of Mariamne and Drusilla, King Agrippa II had cancelled the wedding between Epiphanes and Mariamne, because again Epiphanes refused to adopt the customs and religion of the Jews.'''
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochus_IV_of_Commagene
