1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lucius Cassius Longinus''' was the first husband of the Emperor Caligula's sister Julia Drusilla in 33 AD. Cassius came from an ancient and noble gens, the Cassii. In early 37, he was appointed by Tiberius as a commissioner. Wh
2 CONC en Tiberius died later that year, Caligula became Caesar. Caligula ordered Cassius to divorce Drusilla so that she could marry Marcus Aemilius Lepidus. Caligula subsequently murdered Cassius, before his own assassination in 41, ba
2 CONC sed on an oracle which Caligula interpreted as indicating that Cassius would assassinate him.
2 CONT
2 CONT By a strange coincidence, Caligula was assassinated by a Cassius, the tribune Cassius Chaerea.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wikipedia pages of his father, Lucius Cassius Longinus (cons. 11 AD), in Latin and Spanish state that this Lucius was his son.
2 CONT
