1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Gaius Pomponius Bassus Terentianus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaius Pomponius Bassus Terentianus (fl. 2nd century AD) was a Roman military officer and senator who was appointed suffect consul in around AD 193.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pomponius Bassus Terentianus was a member of the second century gens Pomponia. A successful imperial candidate for the post of quaestor provinciae early in his career, he was later appointed either curator rei publicae of Aquinum 
2 CONC or Urvinum Mataurense. In around AD 185, Terentianus was possibly the Legatus and Iuridicus of Hispania Citerior.
2 CONT
2 CONT In either 186 or 187, Terentianus was the proconsular governor of Lycia et Pamphylia. This was followed by a posting as Legatus Augusti pro praetore of Pannonia Inferior between 187 and 189. Then from around 190 to 192, Terentianu
2 CONC s was a praefectus aerarii militaris (or official responsible for the military treasury) under the emperor Commodus. Finally, sometime around AD 193, he was appointed suffect consul, by one of the reigning emperors (Commodus, Pert
2 CONC inax, Didius Julianus or Septimius Severus).
2 CONT
2 CONT It is possible that Terentianus was the Bassus who was reported as an amicus Severi (or friend of the emperor Septimius Severus). Less likely, he may also have been the Bassus who was Praefectus urbi of Rome for a few weeks during
2 CONC  the reign of Didius Julianus.[3] He was probably the father of Pomponius Bassus who was consul in AD 211.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaius_Pomponius_Bassus_Terentianus
