2 CONT =Manius Laberius Maximus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Manius Laberius Maximus was a Roman statesman who lived during the first and second centuries AD. He was a senator and general under the emperors Domitian and Trajan.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of a family that originated in Lanuvium, where his presumed grandfather, Lucius Laberius Maximus, was a magistrate. His father, also Lucius Laberius Maximus, was a high equestrian official who was successively prae
2 CONC fectus annonae, Prefect of Egypt and Praetorian prefect in the years 80-84. His mother is unknown. Lucius' achievements enabled his son Manius to be adlected to the senatorial order.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maximus was a suffect consul in 89 and is believed to have been Legatus of Numidia before becoming governor of Moesia Inferior in 100-101. (While in Moesia a slave of his, Callidromus, was captured by the Dacians: this man was int
2 CONC erviewed in Bithynia in 111 by Pliny the Younger - see Pliny, Ep., X, 74). Maximus was a general in Trajan's Dacian Wars of 101 and 102 and according to Cassius Dio particularly distinguished himself in the latter campaign. He was
2 CONC  rewarded for his services with a second consulship in 103 as colleague to the Emperor himself, a sign of high favour. This favour did not last. According to Augustan History (Hadrian, V, 5) on the accession of emperor Hadrian in 
2 CONC 117 Maximus was 'in exile on an island under suspicion of designs on the throne'. Nothing more is known of these suspected designs, but they prompted Hadrian's guard prefect Publius Acilius Attianus to recommend Maximus be put to 
2 CONC death. The sequel is not known, but Hadrian was tiring of Attianus and it is more likely that Maximus was pardoned.
2 CONT
2 CONT The identity of Maximus’ wife is unknown. His only known child was a daughter, Laberia Hostilia Crispina. After his death, Crispina became the heiress to his fortune. Crispina became the second wife of Roman consul and senator Gai
2 CONC us Bruttius Praesens Lucius Fulvius Rusticus. She bore him a son, Lucius Fulvius Gaius Bruttius Praesens Laberius Maximus 'Polyonymus', who would also hold the consulship. Maximus was the great-grandfather of the consul Lucius Bru
2 CONC ttius Quintius Crispinus and the Roman empress Bruttia Crispina, who married the Roman Emperor Commodus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
