2 CONT ==Was Mariamne Hasmonean's daughter's name Cypros or Mariamne?==
2 CONT
2 CONT *Cypros, according to Josephus ''The Antiquities of the Jews'', 18.130: Herod the Great had two daughters by Mariamne, the [grand] daughter of Hyrcanus; the one was Salampsio, who was married to Phasaelus, her first cousin, who wa
2 CONC s himself the son of Phasaelus, Herod’s brother, her father making the match; the other was '''Cypros, who was herself married also to her first cousin Antipater, the son of Salome, Herod’s sister'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Cypros, according to Wagner, Sir Anthony Richard; ‘Pedigree and Progress: Essays in the Genealogical Interpretation of History’
2 CONT
2 CONT *Cypros according to Wikipedia: "Mariamne bore Herod four children: two sons, Alexandros and Aristobulus (both executed in 7 BCE), and two daughters, Salampsio and '''Cypros'''. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariamne_I
2 CONT
2 CONT *But Mariamne, according to The Jewish Woman's Archive: "Herod and Mariamme were married for ten years. She bore him five children during those years—his heirs Alexander and Aristobulus, another son who died and two daughters, She
2 CONC lamziyyon and '''Mariamme'''. In 27 B.C.E. Herod had Mariamme executed." http://jwa.org/encyclopedia/article/mariamme-i-hasmonean
2 CONT
2 CONT Until more information can be garnered, I'm presuming Cypros is the Greek name for this daughter, & Mariamne the Hebrew [Sharon Oct 2014 - Please comment on the Discussion]
