2 CONT "Herod the Great had two daughters by Mariamne, the [grand] daughter of Hyrcanus; the one was Salampsio, who was married to Phasaelus, her first cousin, who was himself the son of Phasaelus, Herod's brother, her father making the 
2 CONC match;  the other was Cypros, who was herself married also to her first cousin Antipater, the son of Salome, Herod's sister.  Phasaelus had five children by Salampsio; Antipater, Herod, and Alexander, and two daughters, Alexandra 
2 CONC and Cypros;  which last Agrippa, the son of Aristobulus, married;  and '''Timius of Cyprus married Alexandra; he was a man of note, but had by her no children.'''  Josephus: Antiquities of the Jews XVIII  Chapter 5 .http://religio
2 CONC usstudies.uncc.edu/people/jtabor/john.html
