2 CONT Flavius Josephus' The Jewish War Book 1, Chapter 30:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''When Herod Made Inquiry About Pheroras's Death A Discovery Was Made That Antipater Had Prepared A Poisonous Draught For Him. Herod Casts Doris And Her Accomplices, As Also Mariamne, Out Of The Palace And Blots Her Son Herod Out 
2 CONC Of His Testament''.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. And now it was that he [Herod the Great] betook himself to examine Antipater of Samaria, who was the steward of [his son] Antipater; and upon torturing him, he learned that Antipater had sent for ''a potion of deadly poison for
2 CONC  him out of Egypt, by Antiphilus, a companion of his; that Theudio, the uncle of Antipater, had it from him, and delivered it to Pheroras''; for that Antipater had charged him to take his father off while he was at Rome, and so fr
2 CONC ee him from the suspicion of doing it himself: that Pheroras also committed this potion to his wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation by William Whiston, https://www.josephus.org/works.htm
2 CONT [http://books.google.co.za/books?id=Kk0GAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA462&lpg=PA462&dq=theudion&source=bl&ots=NlLg32LL92&sig=vOLuIZ2poHgLxuaHC8ks0v09kBU&hl=en&sa=X&ei=_SZ0T6nMIcaXhQefxNylBQ&ved=0CEsQ6AEwCA#v=onepage&q=theudion&f=false   Excerpt f
2 CONC rom 'The Works of Flavius Josephus, the Learned and Authentic Jewish Historian ...' By Flavius Josephus]
