2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ROBERT''' [I] ([700/10]-before 764).  The third continuator of the Gesta Abbatum Trudonensium names "Robertus comes vel dux Hasbanie" in 715, and quotes a charter dated 7 Apr 742 under which "Robertus comes, filius condam Lambe
2 CONC rti" donated property "in villa…Sarcinio…in pago Hasbaniensi…[et] Halon, Scaffnis, Felepa et Marholt" to St Trudon[525].  Comte de Hesbaie.  Comes palatinus 741/42.  Graf im Oberrheingau und Wormsgau. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANKSMaiordomi.htm#_Toc359686226
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GRAFEN im WORMSGAU'''
2 CONT A.      Die ROTBERTINER
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ROBERT [I], son of LAMBERT [II] comes in Neustria and Austrasia & his wife --- ([700/10]-before 764).  The third continuator of the Gesta Abbatum Trudonensium names "Robertus comes vel dux Hasbanie" in 715, and quotes a charter
2 CONC  dated 7 Apr 742 under which "Robertus comes, filius condam Lamberti" donated property "in villa…Sarcinio…in pago Hasbaniensi…[et] Halon, Scaffnis, Felepa et Marholt" to St Trudon[501].  Comte de Hesbaie.  Comes palatinus 741/42. 
2 CONC  Graf im Oberrheingau und Wormsgau.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([730]) WILLISWINDA, daughter of ADALHELM Grundherr im Wormsgau & his wife --- (-[12 Jul 764/776]).  "Cancor…Rhenensis pagi comes cum matre sua…Williswinda vidua Ruperti comitis" founded Kloster Lorsch by charter dated 764[502].
2 CONC   "Williswinda…et filius meus Cancor" donated "villam…in pago Wormatiense…Hagenheim super fluvium Salusiam", inherited from "genitoris mei…Adelhelmi", to monastery "Lauresham in pago Rhenense super fluvium Wisgotz" by charter date
2 CONC d 12 Jul 764, signed by "…Heimerici filii Cancronis"[503].  "Heimericus" names "Williswinda avia ipsius Heimericus" in an undated charter relating to a donation to Kloster Lorsch[504].  "Karolus…rex Francorum", in an undated chart
2 CONC er (placed in the compilation with charters dated 772) related to Kloster Lorsch, names "avia…Heimerici…Williswinda vel genitor suus Cancor, germano suo domino Ruodgango archiepiscopo"[505].  The primary source which confirms her 
2 CONC parentage, and that her husband was named Robert, has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert [I] & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         CANCOR (-771).  Graf im Rheingau.  "Cancor…Rhenensis pagi comes cum matre sua…Williswinda vidua Ruperti comitis" founded Kloster Lorsch by charter dated 764[506].  "Williswinda…et filius meus Cancor" donated "villam…in
2 CONC  pago Wormatiense…Hagenheim super fluvium Salusiam", inherited from "genitoris mei…Adelhelmi", to monastery "Lauresham in pago Rhenense super fluvium Wisgotz" by charter dated 12 Jul 764, signed by "…Heimerici filii Cancronis"[507
2 CONC ].  The Chronicon Laureshamense records the donation dated "764 IV Id Iul" in Hagenheim by "Williswinda…et filius meus Cancor comes"[508].  "Cancor et Angila conjux mea" donated property "in illa marcha de Bisistat…de dote Angilæ"
2 CONC  [Birstatt] to Lorsch by charter dated 1 Jun 770, signed by "Thurincberti fratris ipsius Cancronis et Heimerici filii sui"[509].  The Annalium Laureshamensium record the death in 771 of "Cancor"[510].  m ANGILA, daughter of --- (-
2 CONC after 1 Jun 770).  "Cancor et Angila conjux mea" donated property "in illa marcha de Bisistat…de dote Angilæ" [Birstatt] to Lorsch by charter dated 1 Jun 770, signed by "Thurincberti fratris ipsius Cancronis et Heimerici filii sui
2 CONC "[511].  The Chronicon Laureshamense records the donation of "villa Bisistat" dated 1 Jun 770 by "comitis Cancronis et uxoris eius Angila"[512].  Cancor & his wife had [five] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         HEIMRICH [Heimo] (-killed in battle Lüne an der Elbe 5 May 795).  
2 CONT >>b)         [CHRODGANG [Hruotgang] (-after [772]).  
2 CONT >>c)         ERMBERT (-803).  
2 CONT >>d)         RACHILT (-after 1 Nov 792). 
2 CONT >>e)         EUPHEMIA .  
2 CONT
2 CONT >2.         [ANSELM .  Europäische Stammtafeln[525] shows Anselm (-killed in battle Roncesvalles 15 Aug 788), comes palatii, as the son of Robert [I] but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  "Car
2 CONC olus…rex Francorum et Langobardorum" granted the monastery of Plaisir to Folrad abbot of Saint-Denis by charter dated 28 Jul 775 which name "fidelibus…Ghaerardo, Bernardo, Radulfo, Hilderado, Ermenaldo, Hebroino, Theudbaldo, Agneo
2 CONC ne comitibus, Haltberto, Laumberto, Haererico et Anselmo comite palatio nostro"[526].  "Carolus…rex Francorum et Langobardorum" gave a judgment by charter dated to [Dec 775] which names "fidelibus…Widrigo, Odrigo, Theodrico, Berne
2 CONC hardo, Albuino, Aginhardo, Berngario comitibus et Anshelmo comite palacii nostri"[527].  Einhard records that "Eggihardus regiæ mensæ præpositus, Anselmus comes palatii et Hruodlaudus Brittanici limitis præfectus" were killed agai
2 CONC nst “Wascones” having crossed the Pyrenees, dated from the context to the 780s[528].  The epitaph of “Aggiardi” records his death “XVIII Kal Sep”[529], which suggests that the three were killed at the first battle of Roncesvalles,
2 CONC  dated 15 Aug 778.]    
2 CONT
2 CONT >3.         THURINGBERT (-Jun 770 or after).  "Cancor et Angila conjux mea" donated property "in illa marcha de Bisistat…de dote Angilæ" [Birstatt] to Lorsch by charter dated 1 Jun 770, signed by "Thurincberti fratris ipsius Cancr
2 CONC onis et Heimerici filii sui"[530].  The Chronicon Laureshamense records "Thurincberti fratris ipsius Cancronis" as signatory of the donation dated 1 Jun 770 by "comitis Cancronis et uxoris eius Angila"[531].  "Turincbertus" donate
2 CONC d property to Lorsch by charter dated 1 Nov 767 subscribed by "Heimerici comitis"[532].  Grundherr im Rheingau und Wormsgau.  "Turincbertus et filius meus Rotbertus" donated property "in pago Rinensi in villa…Birstat" to Lorsch by
2 CONC  charter dated Jun 770[533].  m ---.  The name of Thuringbert's wife is not known.  Thuringbert & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         ROBERT [II] (-12 Jul 807). 
2 CONT
