2 CONT Einzelnachweise [Bearbeiten]
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ↑ Gerd Tellenbach: Der großfränkische Adel und die Regierung Italiens in der Blütezeit des Karolingerreichs. in: Studien und Vorarbeiten zur Geschichte des Großfränkischen und frühdeutschen Adels. Eberhard Albert Verlag, Fre
2 CONC iburg i. B. 1957, S. 44.
2 CONT    2. ↑ Alfred Friese: Studien zur Herrschaftsgeschichte der fränkischen Adels - Der mainländisch-thüringische Raum vom 7. bis 11. Jahrhundert. Klett-Cotta, Stuttgart 1979, S. 98 ff.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_I._%28Worms-_und_Oberrheingau%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Diese Seite wurde zuletzt am 24. Juni 2010 um 18:34 Uhr geändert.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps04/ps04_357.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ancestral Roots..." (Balt., 1992) 48-13: "Count in the Upper Rhine and Wormgau, seen 722-757; m. Williswint, dau. of Count Adelhelm, wid. 764." Rutpert I is son of Lantbertus (Lambert) II, an adult in ca. 690, dead in 741.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/c/a/u/Jack-Causer/GENE1-0271.html
2 CONT
2 CONT  5123922199552. 
2 CONT ==Robert Count of Hesbaye,== 
2 CONT born Abt. 700 in Hesbaye,Liege,Belgium794; died Aft. 750. He was the son of 5123924037264. Lambert of Hesbaye and 5123924037265. Chrotlinde of the Franks. He married 5123922199553. Williswinda Abt. 719. 
2 CONT
2 CONT       5123922199553. Williswinda, born Abt. 700; died Unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Robert Hesbaye and Williswinda is: 
2 CONT   2561961099776 i.   Guerin Count in the Thurgovie, born Abt. 720 in Hesbaye,Liege,Belgium; died 20 May 772; married Adelindis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://craveirolopes.familytreeguide.com/getperson.php?personID=I197&tree=T1
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://sbaldw.home.mindspring.com/hproject/prov/rober100.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert "le Fort" (Rotbertus Fortis, Robert "the Strong")..........
2 CONT
2 CONT Probable father: Robert, d. before 19 February 834, count in Wormsgau.
2 CONT  Probable mother: Waldrade (Wialdrut), living 19 February 834....
2 CONT
2 CONT He was evidently the count Robert whose son Robert donated two manses in Mettenheim in 8367 [Codex Lauresh., 2: 306-7 (#1826), see above]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Attempts at further identification of this Robert suffer from the possibility of confusing different men with the same name. On 8 March 812, a count Rotbertus appears with several other counts in a court record of Charlemagne [MGH
2 CONC  DD KdG, 289 (#216)]. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT The cartulary of Lorsch shows a count Robert in Wormsgau on 12 June 795 ["... ego Rubertus comes ...", Codex Lauresh., 2: 236 (#1541)] and in Rheingau on 25 March 804 ["... signum Rutperti comitis, ..." ibid., 1: 318 (#222)] and o
2 CONC n 20 February 807 ["... signum Rutperti comitis..." ibid., 1: 319 (#224)].
2 CONT
2 CONT  Glöckner would identify him as Robert "II" and make him the father of Robert "III" (with no direct evidence for the affiliation). 
2 CONT
2 CONT This Robert "II" would then be identified by Glöckner as "probably" the same as the Robert son of Turimbert who appears in the Lorsch cartulary in 769770 ["... ego Turinebertus, & filius meus Ruotpertus, ..." ibid., 1: 285 (#168)]
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Turimbert does not have a title in the documents in which he appears, and Robert son of Turimbert also appears without a title, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Turincbert was the son of a count Robert "I", whose son Cancor and widow Williswinte founded Lorsch in 764 [see Glöckner (1936), 303-5; Codex Lauresh., 1: 2], which is why  Glöckner would identify Turimbert's son as Robert "II" [G
2 CONC löckner (1936), 305]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On the other hand, Siegwart does not accept the identification of Robert "II" with Robert son of Turimbert, and instead makes Robert "II" the son of a Robert "I" (different from the Robert "I" of Glöckner), son of count Hnabi who 
2 CONC was the maternal grandfather of Hildegard, wife of Charlemagne [Siegwart (1958), 157]
2 CONT
2 CONT Chaume regarded the Robert "II" and "III" of Glöckner as a single count Robert of Rheingau (fl. 795-834, whose son Robert, fl. 836-7, he regarded as distinct from Robert le Fort), in turn a conjectured son of count Heimrich, son o
2 CONC f count Cancor, son of count Robert and Williswinte [Chaume (1925), 537 (table #5)].  ....
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Graf in Wormsgau and Upper-Rhine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo:  Europäische Stammtafeln, Band II, Frank Baron Freytag von Loringhoven, 1975, Isenburg, W. K. Prinz von, Reference: Page 13.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo: Genealogisches Handbuch des Adels, Fürstliche Häuser , Reference: 1961, 9.
2 CONT --------------------
