2 CONT >*'''[https://www.geni.com/people/Thuringbert-of-Hesbaye-Graf-im-Wormsgau/6000000031944863426?through=6000000001745043673 THURINGBERT] (-Jun 770 or >) "Cancor et Angila conjux mea" donated property "in illa marcha de Bisistat…de d
2 CONC ote Angilæ" [Birstatt] to Lorsch by charter dated 1 Jun 770, signed by "Thurincberti fratris ipsius Cancronis et Heimerici filii sui"[530].  The Chronicon Laureshamense records "Thurincberti fratris ipsius Cancronis" as signatory 
2 CONC of the donation dated 1 Jun 770 by "comitis Cancronis et uxoris eius Angila"[531].  "Turincbertus" donated property to Lorsch by charter dated 1 Nov 767 subscribed by "Heimerici comitis"[532].  Grundherr im Rheingau und Wormsgau. 
2 CONC  "Turincbertus et filius meus Rotbertus" donated property "in pago Rinensi in villa…Birstat" to Lorsch by charter dated Jun 770[533].  m ---.  The name of Thuringbert's wife is not known.  Thuringbert & his wife had one child:'''
2 CONT >>*a)         ROBERT [II] (-12 Jul 807).  "Turincbertus et filius meus Rotbertus" donated property "in pago Rinensi in villa…Birstat" to Lorsch by charter dated Jun 770[534].  Graf im Wormsgau und Oberrheingau 795/807.  Herr zu Di
2 CONC enheim 795.  [same person as…?  RADBERT (-807).  Einhard records that "Radbertus missus imperatoris" died in 807 after returning from the Orient[535].  It is possible that "Radbertus" refers to "Rodbertus".] 
2 CONT
