2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cancor
2 CONT
2 CONT Cancor was a Frankish count, possibly of Hesbaye.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 764 he founded Lorsch Abbey together with his widowed mother [http://www.geni.com/people/Williswinda-von-Wormsgau/6000000002187572021 Williswinda] as a proprietary church and monastery on their estate, Laurissa. They entrusted 
2 CONC its government to Cancor's nephew [http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Chrodegang-de-Metz/6000000008462307502 Chrodegang], Archbishop of Metz, son of Cancor's sister [http://www.geni.com/people/Landrada-von-Worms-Rheingau/60000000039
2 CONC 37185753 Landrada]. Chrodegang dedicated the church and monastery to Saint Peter and became its first abbot. The founders enriched the new abbey later by further donations.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 766 Chrodegang resigned the office of abbot owing to his other important duties as Archbishop of Metz. He then sent his brother [http://www.geni.com/people/Gundeland/6000000023711178084 Gundeland], another nephew of Cancor, to 
2 CONC Lorsch as his successor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cancor is probably related to the Robertians. His father's name may have been [http://www.geni.com/people/Robert-I-count-in-Wormsgau-Upper-Rheingau/6000000001745043673 Rodbert]. Robert and [http://www.geni.com/people/Ingeramne-cou
2 CONC nt-of-Hesbaye/6000000008858884656 Ingram of Hesbaye] may have been his brothers, which implies that [http://www.geni.com/people/Ermengarde-de-Hesbaye/6000000005792904234 Ermengard], wife of emperor [http://www.geni.com/people/Empe
2 CONC ror-Louis-I-The-Pious-son-of-Charlemagne-Hildegard/6000000001266578142 Louis the Pious], was his niece. Therefore he may have been related to the Carolingian royal house
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Sources
