1 NOTE Cancor was a Frankish count, possibly of Hesbaye.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 764 he founded Lorsch Abbey together with his widowed mother Williswinda as a proprietary church and monastery on their estate, Laurissa. They entrusted its government to Cancor's nephew Chrodegang, Archbishop of Metz, son of C
2 CONC ancor's sister Landrada. Chrodegang dedicated the church and monastery to Saint Peter and became its first abbot. The founders enriched the new abbey later by further donations.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 766 Chrodegang resigned the office of abbot owing to his other important duties as Archbishop of Metz. He then sent his brother Gundeland, another nephew of Cancor, to Lorsch as his successor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cancor is probably related to the Robertians. His father's name may have been Rodbert. Robert and Ingram of Hesbaye may have been his brothers, which implies that Ermengard, wife of emperor Louis the Pious, was his niece. Therefor
2 CONC e he may have been related to the Carolingian royal house
