1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marcus Aemilius Lepidus (executed 39)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT For other persons named Marcus Aemilius Lepidus, see Marcus Aemilius Lepidus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Aemilius Lepidus, (6-39) was the son of consul Lucius Aemilius Paullus.[1] His older sister Aemilia Lepida was married to Emperor Caligula's elder brother Drusus Caesar. [2] He was also great-grandson of Lucius Aemilius Lep
2 CONC idus Paullus (consul of 50 BC and brother of the triumvir Marcus Aemilius Lepidus). Some areas of his lineage are unclear. However, through his mother Julia the Younger, Lepidus was the great grandson of Emperor Augustus Caesar. [
2 CONC 3] Lepidus married Caligula's sister Drusilla sometime in November or December of 37.[4] Little is known about him prior to this.[5] Drusilla had been married to Lucius Cassius Longinus since 33 but the couple was ordered to divor
2 CONC ce by the emperor, so that she could marry Lepidus.[4] The marriage lasted until Drusilla's death in June of 38. They had no children. Because of this marriage, Lepidus had become a close friend to Caligula and his family.[6] Afte
2 CONC r the death of Gemellus in 37, Lepidus was publicly marked by Caligula as his heir.[7] In late 38, when the governor of Egypt Aulus Avilius Flaccus was arrested, Lepidus successfully persuaded Caligula to exile Flaccus to Andros r
2 CONC ather than Gyarus.[8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT However, this good-standing did not last. Sometime in 39, Caligula made public letters by his sisters Agrippina and Livilla that detailed an adulterous affair with Lepidus and a plot against the emperor.[10] Lepidus was executed a
2 CONC nd Caligula's sisters were exiled. Agrippina was given the bones of Lepidus in an urn, and she carried them to Rome.[11] Caligula sent three daggers to the Temple of Mars the Avenger to celebrate the death. In the Senate, Vespasia
2 CONC n made a motion that the remains of Lepidus be thrown away instead of buried. The motion was carried and Lepidus was not given a proper burial.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Aemilius_Lepidus_(executed_39)
2 CONT
