1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aemilia_Lepida#Aemilia_Lepida_.28d._36.29.2C_wife_of_the_imperial_prince_Drusus
2 CONT
2 CONT =Aemilia Lepida (d. 36), wife of the imperial prince Drusus=
2 CONT '''Aemilia Lepida''' (d. 36) was daughter of '''Marcus Aemilius Lepidus''', consul in 6 and niece to the consul '''Lucius Aemilius Paullus''' (executed 14 AD). Despite her uncle's disgrace, and due to her father's high standing wi
2 CONC th the Roman emperors and the Senate, she married her second cousin '''Drusus Caesar'''. Tacitus reports that during their marriage "she had pursued her husband with ceaseless accusations". In 36, she was charged with adultery wit
2 CONC h a slave and committed suicide, "since there was no question about her guilt" (Annals 6.40).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Aemilia Lepida=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Aemilia Lepida (died 36) was daughter of Marcus Aemilius Lepidus, consul in 6 and niece to the consul Lucius Aemilius Paullus (executed 14 AD). Despite her uncle's disgrace, and due to her father's high standing with the Roman emp
2 CONC erors and the Senate, she married her second cousin Drusus Caesar. Tacitus reports that during their marriage "she had pursued her husband with ceaseless accusations". In 36, she was charged with adultery with a slave and committe
2 CONC d suicide, "since there was no question about her guilt" (Annals 6.40).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aemilia_Lepida#Aemilia_Lepida_.28died_36.29.2C_wife_of_Drusus
