2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Faustus Cornelius Sulla=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Faustus Cornelius Sulla (before 86-46 BC) was a Roman senator. Faustus was the only surviving son of the Dictator of Rome Lucius Cornelius Sulla and his fourth wife Caecilia Metella, and thus a member of one of the most ancient pa
2 CONC trician families, the Cornelii. After his father's death in 78 BC, he and his twin sister Fausta were brought up by his guardian, his father's friend Lucullus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Faustus married Pompeia, daughter of Pompey the Great. Faustus accompanied Pompey on his Asian campaigns, and was the first to climb over the walls of the Temple of Jerusalem when it was stormed by Pompey in 63 BC. After his retur
2 CONC n to Rome, he gave gladiatorial games to celebrate his father in 60 BC. At an unknown time before 57 BC, Faustus Sulla became augur. As moneyer in 56 BC, he issued coinage in honor of his father and his father-in-law. As owner of 
2 CONC the central slopes of Mount Falernus, his name became synonymous with the most esteemed wine in ancient Rome, Faustian Falernian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Faustus Sulla was Quaestor in 54 BC. The senate commissioned him to rebuild the Curia Hostilia in 52 BC which had been burned down after the riots which followed the murder of Clodius. After that the Curia was known as the Curia C
2 CONC ornelia.
2 CONT
2 CONT His career as an advocate was cut short, however, by the Civil War between Pompey and Julius Caesar. He, as Lucullus' ward and Pompey's son-in-law, sided with the former. Faustus was at the Battle of Pharsalus in 48 BC, joining th
2 CONC e leaders of his party in Africa subsequently. After the Battle of Thapsus, he tried to escape to Mauretania, but was caught and killed by Publius Sittius, a supporter of Caesar, in 46 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT With Pompeia he had at least two children: Faustus Cornelius Sulla the Younger (later became suffect consul) and Cornelia Sulla (married a Lucius Scribonius Libo, who was praetor in 80 BC). From one of whom is presumably descended
2 CONC  Faustus Cornelius Sulla, suffect consul in 31 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faustus_Cornelius_Sulla_(senator)
