2 CONT '''Sextus Pompeius Magnus Pius,''' in English Sextus Pompey (67 BC-35 BC),[1] was a Roman general from the late Republic (1st century BC). He was the last focus of opposition to the Second Triumvirate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sextus Pompeius was the youngest son of Pompey the Great (Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus)[1] by his third wife, Mucia Tertia. His older brother was Gnaeus Pompeius, from the same mother. Both boys grew up in the shadow of their father, on
2 CONC e of Rome's best generals and an originally non-conservative politician who drifted to the more traditional faction when Julius Caesar became a threat.
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Sextus had married Scribonia, a distant relative of his. Scribonia was the daughter of Lucius Scribonius Libo, consul of 34 BC. Sextus and Scribonia had a daughter and only child called Pompeia Magna.
