2 CONT Better known by his nickname Caligula (/kəˈlɪɡjʊlə/), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Roman emperor from AD 37 until his assassination in AD 41. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of the Roman general Germanicus and Augustus' granddaughter Agrippina the Elder,
2 CONT
2 CONT  members of the first ruling family of the Roman Empire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born two years before Tiberius was made emperor. Gaius accompanied his father, mother and siblings on campaign in Germania, at little more than four or five years old. He had been named after Gaius Julius Caesar, but his fa
2 CONC ther's soldiers affectionately nicknamed him "Caligula" ('little boot').
