2 CONT
2 CONT -Julia Caesaris "Maior" (the elder)
2 CONT
2 CONT -Julia Caesaris "Minor" (the younger)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Wives
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''First marriage to''''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Cornelia Cinnilla, from 83 BC until her death in childbirth in 69 or 68 BC
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Second marriage to''''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Pompeia, from 67 BC until he divorced her around 61 BC
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Third marriage to''''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Calpurnia Pisonis, from 59 BC until Caesar's death
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Julia with Cornelia Cinnilla, born in 83 or 82 BC
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Caesarion, with Cleopatra VII, born 47 BC. He was killed at age 17 by Caesar's adopted son Octavianus.
2 CONT
2 CONT -adopted: Gaius Julius Caesar Octavianus, his great-nephew by blood, who later became Emperor Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Junius Brutus: The historian Plutarch notes that Caesar believed Brutus to have been his illegitimate son, as his mother Servilia had been Caesar's lover during their youth.[128]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Grandchildren
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandson from Julia and Pompey, dead at several days, unnamed.
2 CONT
