2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Laberius Maximus (date of birth or death unknown) was a Roman governor of the Egypt province in 83, and prefect of the imperial bodyguard, known as the Praetorian Guard, during the reign of emperor Domitian, in 84. Prior to
2 CONC  achieving these positions, Laberius Maximus had also successfully completed a term as Praefectus annonae, or the prefect in charge of the grain supply of Rome. With this career, Maximus distinguished himself by attaining the high
2 CONC est offices open to Romans of the equestrian class.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son was Manius Laberius Maximus, a significant senator and military figure during the reigns of the emperors Domitian and Trajan.
2 CONT
2 CONT   This Ancient Roman biographical article is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it. 
2 CONT
