2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p12/74/45/4b/94/534448386cd3080d/picroute-00096-3_original.jpg?hash=71d309e054df797bcc47c1895107435affe36b2c314251c9bc3d1795bfd4e707.1793865599
2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE Start - Killevy Churches
3 CONT Killevy (from Ir. Cill Shléibhe, 'church of the mountain') is situated at the foot of Slieve Gullion on its NE side. It is the site of an early convent founded at the end of the 5th century by a female saint known variously as Dar
3 CONC erca, Moninna or Bline. According to tradition she was baptised and confirmed by St. Patrick. How is it possible that one woman had three names? The answer is that Darerca was her original name, while Moninna was a pet name given 
3 CONC by those who venerated her, a common enough phenomenon with Irish saints. Bline is a further development of Moninna, whereby the consonants mn became bl. A granite slab at the northern end of the graveyard, recently cleaned up and
3 CONC  inscribed with her name, marks her resting place. Nothing remains of the early convent. The later church that stands on its site is in fact two churches, joined together to form one long building. The earliest part is the lintell
3 CONC ed door of the west church dating to the 10th or 11th century.
