2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT Alternate spellings: Welsh-Cadfan, Latin-Catamanus, English-Gideon, Gadeon
2 CONT
2 CONT Conan was a real figure whose actual story was modified over the centuries by re-telling into various legends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Story: Gadeon appears in the Dream of Macsen Wledig as brother of King Conan Meriadoc of Dumnonia & Brittany, though he actually seems to have been his son by St. Ursula , presumably born in Rome. Upon the death of his father, Gad
2 CONC eon inherited a position of some power and influence in the Civitas Dumnoniorum, his mother's homeland, while his half-brother, Gradlon (alias Urban), took on Armorica (Brittany). He may have become the decurion of Isca Dumnonioru
2 CONC m (modern Exeter), where he probably died around AD 405. His place in society was inherited by his son, Guoremor .
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.britannia.com/bios/ebk/gadeodm.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Ystrafael
2 CONT
2 CONT Gwrfawr (~358-~415)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Adeon mab Eudaf
2 CONT
2 CONT Jesus College MS20 genealogy of the children of Cunedda gives their mother as Gwawl daughter of Coel Hen. The wife of Coel Hen being the daughter of Gadeon son of Eudaf Hen. This Gadeon is the same as Adeon indicating that he marr
2 CONC ied on his return to Britain and was considered a progenitor of the royal house of Gwynedd.
2 CONT
