2 CONT In stories:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Cymri hero, also known as Adeon mab Eudaf
2 CONT
2 CONT This hero is known from the Mabinogi of The Dream of Magnus Maximus (Breuddwyud Macsen Wledig) and is one of Magnus Maximus companions on his way to subdue Rome. Adeon returns to found the Royal House of Gwynedd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeon mab Eudaf is from this source: the Mabinogion of Breuddwyd Macsen Wledig. In the tale Magnus Maximus, emperor of Rome, has a dream where he sees a magnificent castle. Within the castle there is a great hall and in this hall 
2 CONC two youths are playing gwyddbwyll using a silver board. Beside a pillar in the hall he saw a hoary-headed man sitting before a golden gwyddbwyll board and carving pieces with a file from a rod of gold. Before this man sat a maiden
2 CONC  in a chair of ruddy gold. She was the fairest maiden that he had ever seen. Magnus Maximus instantly falls in love with the maiden and urged by his counsellors he sends messengers to seek her out. Finally she is found and Magnus 
2 CONC Maximus assembles his host and ventures forth to gain her hand.
2 CONT
2 CONT He voyaged to Britain and in Arfon he saw the castle where he saw the two youths, Cynan mab Eudaf and Adeon mab Eudaf playing gwyddbwyll and he saw Eudaf mab Caradog sitting in his ivory chair carving chessmen. There he saw the ma
2 CONC iden, hailing her. The next day she asked him for her maiden portion, which was the Island of Britain to be held by her father for her from the channel to the Irish Sea and she would have three castles made for her; the first and 
2 CONC greatest in Arfon (which would become known as Caernarfon), the second Caerleon and the third at Caerfyrddin. Magnus Maximus wins Elen's hand and tarries in her realm for seven years. By which time, according to the laws of Rome a
2 CONC  new emperor has been created. Hearing of this in a missive Maximus raises his host and marches on Rome, subduing each realm as he passes. But Rome herself proves impregnable and he camps before her walls for a full year before he
2 CONC  seen a host approach. This host is led by Cynan and Eudaf. They avowed to attack the city and gain it for Magnus Maximus. By night they measured the height of the walls and had their carpenters form ladders, enough for every four
2 CONC  men in their company. In the morning the men of Britain took their food, and they drank until they were invigorated. At noon, when the fighting ceased and the two emperors went to meat the Brython came to the city and placing the
2 CONC ir ladders against the wall they scaled these and made their way into Rome. The new emperor had not even enough time to arm himself when they fell upon him and slew him. A full three nights and three days were they subduing Rome a
2 CONC nd they kept guard at the walls to prevent Maximus from entering until they had subjected all to their will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Within time Maximus spoke to Elen, saying that her brothers (Cynan and Adeon) had not subdued the city for him. But she replied that her brothers were the wisest youths in the entire world and that he should venture forth and ask 
2 CONC the city of them. If it was in their possession it would gladly be given to him. Maximus and Elen went to the city and demanded it. But the citizens said that none could do this but the men of the Island of Britain. Then were the 
2 CONC gates opened to them and Maximus was hailed emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT In payment for what they had done Cynan and Adeon were given any region they desired in the world to vanquish and hold as their own. Thus they came to the land of Armorica where they slew all the men and kept the women, subduing t
2 CONC he land to their will. When this was done Cynan spoke to Adeon asking him whether he would remain in this new land or return to his own home. Adeon chose to return to the land of the Brython whilst Cynan stayed in Armorica to foun
2 CONC d the land of Llydaw (Brittany).
