1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Antipater the Idumaean [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antipater_the_Idumaean Wikipedia] (d. 43 BC) was the founder of the Herodian Dynasty and father of Herod the Great. According to Africanus and Epiphanius, he was
2 CONC  the son of Herod (I) of Ascalon. According to Josephus, he was the son of Antipas (I).
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal details
2 CONT
2 CONT Antipater was married to Cypros, a Nabataean noblewoman. They had four sons: Phasael, Herod, Joseph, and Pheroras, and a daughter, Salome, one of several Salomes among the Herodians.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT See [http://www.geni.com/discussions/151163?msg=1053520 Discussion] of his birthdate
