2 CONT
2 CONT === Theidlindis of Blois
2 CONT * French: Theudelinde de Bliesgau 
2 CONT * Gender:	Female 
2 CONT * Birth:	estimated between 752 and 770 - Blois, Loir-et-Cher, Centre, France 
2 CONT * Death:	circa 795 - France 
2 CONT * Daughter of Aubri II, Count of Blois and an unknown woman 
2 CONT * Wife of Gainfroi, count of Sens  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''from Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnulf of Sens(ca.793/794 - April, 841) was a Frankish noble, an illegitimate son of Louis the Pious, the son of Charlemagne. His mother Theodelinde of Sens (ca.764 - 794) was the daughter of '''Gainfroi, count of Sens''' and '''T
2 CONC heidlindis de Blois'''. He had one sister, Alpaïs de Paris, abbess of St-Pierre de Reims. In 794 A.D., Arnulf's mother Theodelinde of Sens was dead. In 817 Arnulf was appointed count of Sens in Burgundy. He was the first son of Lo
2 CONC uis the Pious, but he did not inherit land because he was illegitimate. In April 841 A.D., he died at Sens before the Treaty of Verdun.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(Theislinda)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT HM George I s 23-oldemor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HRE Ferdinand I s 20-oldemor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Amerikanske præsidents 26-oldemor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto von Bismarcks 27-oldemor.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Agnes Harris '26-oldemor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Husband / Partner:       Gainfroi (Count) von MESSGAU 
2 CONT Child:       Giselbert (Count) von MESSGAU (Moselle)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hendes (evt.) 2-oldebørn:       Regnier (Rainier Reginar) II (Count) af Hainaut   ,   Giselbert (Hainaut) (Duke) de Lothringen   ,   Simphoriane af Hainaut   ,   Erenfried I (Count) von Bliesgau 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disproved pedigree 
2 CONT
2 CONT Older sources show her with a disproved ancestry.  From http://www.rpi.edu/~holmes/Hobbies/Genealogy/ps04/ps04_456.htm (defunct link); “descends from the Merovingian Kings of France (Clovis I the Great and his wife St. Clothilda),
2 CONC  etc. - her ancestry reaches back to Clodion, King of the Salic Franks (ca. 380-448).”  See the profile https://www.geni.com/people/Adela/6000000222648329906 for discussion.  
2 CONT
