2 CONC ’s position as the only son of Caesar, and war was inevitable. He defeated Antony and Cleopatra’s forces in a naval battle off Actium in 31 bc; they both killed themselves the following year. Caesarion was murdered. In 29 bc Octav
2 CONC ian returned to Rome in triumph, at age 34 the sole master of the Roman world.
