2 CONT '''Marcus Livius Drusus (consul 15 BC)'''
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Marcus Livius Drusus I was the son of praetor Marcus Livius Drusus Claudianus and Aufidia. He was born in 52 BC, in Rome. He was the younger brother of Rome's first Empress Livia Drusilla, and brother-in-law of Roman Emperor Augus
2 CONC tus. He was also the maternal uncle to Roman Emperor Tiberius and General Nero Claudius Drusus. His paternal grandfather was the tribune Marcus Livius Drusus I. His maternal grandmother is unknown, while his maternal grandfather w
2 CONC as the Roman Magistrate Marcus Aufidius Lurco. He was the namesake of his grandfather and his nephew Nero Claudius Drusus was named after him. Very little is known on his life. Livius Drusus served as an aedile in 28 BC, shortly b
2 CONC efore the Pantheon in Rome was completed. He served as a consul in 15 BC. Historian Pliny the Elder (H.N. xxxvi. 15. s. 24), mentions him among those in Rome, who hosted the Secular Games, during Augustus’ reign.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Livius_Drusus_(consul_15_BC)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died : 91 BC 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died : 91 BC 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died : 91 BC 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died : 91 BC 
