1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Erich, King of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT (born c.425)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Welsh-Gereint, Latin-Ericius, English-Eric)
2 CONT
2 CONT King Rivod's uncle, Erich, may have held the Breton throne for a short time in his twilight years. It has been suggested that he was the original Eric in the tale of "Eric and Enid" that the Welsh later transformed into a story co
2 CONC ncerning King Gerren (alias Gereint) of Dumnonia as "Gereint and Enid". King Erich died in 478 and was succeeded by his son, Budic II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Brittany Erich ab Aldrien of Brittany1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 425, d. 478
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	King of Brittany Aldrien ap Selyfan of Brittany1 b. circa 373, d. 464
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	N. N. of Ireland2 b. circa 400
2 CONT
2 CONT      King of Brittany Erich ab Aldrien of Brittany was known, in Welsh, as Gereint; in Latin, Ericius; and in English, Eric.3 He was King Rivod's uncle.3 He was born circa 425.3 He was the son of King of Brittany Aldrien ap Selyfa
2 CONC n of Brittany and N. N. of Ireland.1,2 King of Brittany Erich ab Aldrien of Brittany may have held the Breton throne for a short time in his twilight years.3 King of Brittany before 478.1 He died in 478.1,4
2 CONT
