2 CONT =Sextus Appuleius III=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sextus Appuleius III was the son of the previous and Quinctilia. This Sextus Appuleius was also a half-great-nephew of Augustus via his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT His career is largely unknown, except that he became ordinary consul in the year 14.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was during his consulship in 14, that his half-great-uncle, Augustus, died and was succeeded by Tiberius. As a magistrate, Appuleius was the first to swear allegiance to Tiberius.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Fabia Numantina, a daughter of either Africanus Fabius Maximus, or Paullus Fabius Maximus and Marcia, a maternal cousin of Augustus (daughter of Atia, his aunt, and his step-brother Philippus).
2 CONT
2 CONT Appuleius and Fabia had one son, also named Sextus Appuleius (IV).
2 CONT
2 CONT It is assumed he died not long after 14 because he is not mentioned subsequent to his consulship. His death is not recorded by Tacitus in the surviving part of The Annals, suggesting that it occurred during the period covered in b
2 CONC ook 5 or after book 6. He was survived by his wife Fabia Numantina and their daughter Appuleia Varilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sextus_Appuleius
