2 CONT =Family Background & Early Life=
2 CONT
2 CONT Asiaticus was of Praetorian rank.[2] He was the son born to the Roman Senator, consul Decimus Valerius Asiaticus[3] and the Roman noblewoman Lollia Saturnina. There is a possibility he may have had other siblings. He and along wit
2 CONC h his family were originated from Vienna,[4] Gallia Narbonensis.
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of Asiaticus was of Allobrogian origin[5] and his political career was a contemporary of the rule of the Roman emperors Tiberius, Caligula and Claudius. His father was a respected,[6] wealthy, and prominent Roman Senato
2 CONC r.[7] The elder Asiaticus in 35 served as a suffect consul and again in 46, served as an ordinary consul.[8] He was the first citizen from Vienna to become consul,[9] the first man from Gaul to attain the consulship[10] and became
2 CONC  the first man from Gaul to be admitted into the Roman Senate.[11] The elder Asiaticus had a brother who served as a Roman Senator until 47.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT The mother of Asiaticus was the social, beautiful woman Lollia Saturnina,[13] whose younger sister Lollia Paulina was a Roman empress and the third wife of the Roman emperor Caligula.[14] Saturnina was the first daughter of the su
2 CONC ffect consul Marcus Lollius and the noble woman Volusia Saturnina,[15] as she was a first cousin to Roman emperor Tiberius and his brother, the General Nero Claudius Drusus.[16]
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Asiaticus was the namesake of his father and through Roman citizenship he was a member of the gens Valeria, through his mother he also had relations to that gens. His maternal grandfather Marcus Lollius, was the son born 
2 CONC to the Roman Politician and Military Officer Marcus Lollius[17] from his wife Valeria.[18] Valeria was one of the daughters of the literary patron, consul Marcus Valerius Messalla Corvinus and a sister to the Roman Senators Marcus
2 CONC  Valerius Messalla Messallinus and Marcus Aurelius Cotta Maximus Messalinus.[19] His father was murdered on the orders of the Roman empress Valeria Messalina in 47[20] and was later raised by his mother. Little is known on his ear
2 CONC ly life.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Political career=
2 CONT
2 CONT After serving as a Legatus of Gallia Belgica,[21] he later became the Roman governor of that province[22] in the reign of the Roman emperor Nero.[23] In early 69 when Aulus Vitellius became Roman emperor, he was finding governors 
2 CONC and commanders in the provinces as supporters for his emperorship who were genuinely enthusiastic.[24] Among those supporters was Asiaticus.[25] When Vitellius was in the city of Lugdunum Gaul,[26] proclaiming his son and daughter
2 CONC  as heirs from his wife Galeria Fundana,[27] Vitellius betrothed his daughter Vitellia to Asiaticus.[28] Asiaticus and Vitellia had married in the reign of Vitellius.[29]
2 CONT
2 CONT He had become powerful through wealth and the skilful exploitation of imperial patronage.[30] The alliance with Asiaticus and Vitellius was perhaps an attempt to reconcile the communities in Gaul with the Roman state.[31] Asiaticu
2 CONC s was unable to give Vitellius much support when the Roman army commanders appointed, Vespasian as an alternative successor to Vitellius.[32]
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vespasian became Roman emperor in second half of 69, Asiaticus was appointment for a consulship in 70.[33] Before he could serve his consulship in early 70, Asiaticus died.[34]
2 CONT
2 CONT Asiaticus was survived by Vitellia and their son Marcus Lollius Paulinus Decimus Valerius Asiaticus Saturninus.[35] Later in 70, Vespasian arranged Vitellia to remarry another unnamed groom.[36] Her second marriage was a splendid 
2 CONC match for her and Vespasian provided for her, the dowry and clothing.[37]
2 CONT
