2 CONC 41 married to Berthe de SAINT RIQUIER, De Saint Riquier with : F Bertha de BOULOGNE, De Boulogne ca 893
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wigerich, also Widericus, Windericus, Widiacus''' (* 870, † before 922) was an early medieval count in the Duchy of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wigerich (Widiacus)''' is mentioned in 899 in a issued in Trier royal letter Zwentibolds as important count ( comes venerabilis). [1] He had Count's authority over the city of Trier, as is clear from a document of Louis the Chi
2 CONC ld yields of 19 September 902. FIG. [2] He was also 902 and 909 '''Count in Bidgau''' [3] and from 915/916 '''Palatine of''' '''Lorraine''' as one in the '''Palatinate to Herstal''' created charter of Charles the Simple occupied. 
2 CONC [4] Furthermore, had the Wigeric of Lotharingia Vogteienon the Saint Rumoldus Abbey in Mechelen (as a fief of the Bishop of Liège) and the monastery of Hastière , which were confirmed to him and his son Adalberon by a document dra
2 CONC wn between 911 and 915 Charles the Simple. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wigerich was brother of Abbot Friedrich von Gorze and Verdun ( Saint Vanne ). Maybe Wigerich was a son of Count Odacar ( Ardennergau , Bidgau and Bliesgau ). In any case, he is considered the progenitor of the Ardennes counts ( Wi
2 CONC geriche ).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wigerich was married to Kunigunde''' (* 890/895), a granddaughter of Ludwig der Stammler and possibly a daughter of Reginar I. von Hainegau ( Reginare ).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He founded the Abbey of Hastière , where he was probably also buried'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Wigerich and Kunigunde are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gozelo (* around 914, † April 19, 942); ⚭ 930 Uda (* 905, † April 10, 963) daughter of Count Gerhard ( Matfriede ) Adalbero I (* 910, † April 26, 962), Bishop of Metz 929-962 Siegfried I. (* 915/917, † October 26, 997), count in M
2 CONC oselgau Frederick I (* 912, 17 June 978), Count of Bar and 959 Duke of Oberlothringen Giselbert, count in the Ardennesgau
2 CONT
2 CONT Remarks : Are often regarded as children of Wigerich: Liutgard (* 915, attested on April 8, 960 [6] ); ⚭ I Adalbert († 944) Count of Metz ( Matfriede ); ⚭ II Eberhard von Egisheim († 972/973) and her brother Heinrich (mentioned 97
2 CONC 0 [7] ). There are apparently children of '''Wigeric of Lotharingia''', son of Roric, testified (these two "Ardennes-Verdun dynasty" are 909 as contemporaries quoted in the territory of Count Wigeric of Lotharingia Bidgau [8] ).
