2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hoel I Mawr, King of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT (born c.491)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Welsh-Hywel, Latin-Hovelius, English-Howel)
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Brittany Hoël I Mawr ap Budic de Bretagne1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 491, d. 545
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Emyr Llydaw Budic II map Erich of Brittany1 b. circa 460, d. 544
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Queen of Garlot Elaine verch Gorles o Cernyw1 b. circa 475
2 CONT
2 CONT      Also called Hywel ap Budig Welsh. Also called Hovelius filius Budicius Latin.1 Also called Howel I "the Great" English, Mawr = the Great.1 King of Brittany Hoël I Mawr ap Budic de Bretagne was born circa 491.1 He was the son 
2 CONC of Emyr Llydaw Budic II map Erich of Brittany and Queen of Garlot Elaine verch Gorles o Cernyw.1 King of Brittany Hoël I Mawr ap Budic de Bretagne married Alma Pompea verch Riatham of Dumnonée, daughter of Prince of Dumnonée Rioth
2 CONC am ap Deroch of Dumnonée, before 520; 3rd cousins, 1x removed.1 King of Brittany Hoël I Mawr ap Budic de Bretagne a great supporter of his uncle King Arthur of Britain lending his support to many campaigns, including that to Paris
2 CONC .2 King of Brittany at France in 545. He died in 545.1,3
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Alma Pompea verch Riatham of Dumnonée b. circa 485
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Brittany Tewdr Mawr ap Hoël de Bretagne+ b. c 5201
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Brittany Hoël II Fychan ap Hoël de Bretagne+ b. c 522, d. 5471
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S266] EBK, online http://freespace.virgin.net/david.ford2/…
2 CONT
2 CONT [S266] EBK, online http://freespace.virgin.net/david.ford2/…, per Geoffrey of Monmouth.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S278] DfAdam, online unknown url, The Line of Caradoc, Lord of Meiriadog, 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hoël was also called Hywel ap Budig (Welsh). and also Hovelius filius Budicius (Latin), and also Howel I "the Great" (English; Mawr = the Great).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hoël married his third cousin once removed Alma Pompea verch Riatham of Dumnonée, daughter of Prince of Dumnonée Riotham ap Deroch of Dumnonée, before 520.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was supposedly a great supporter of his uncle King Arthur of Britain, lending his support to many campaigns, including that to Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was King of Brittany in France in 545.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p292.htm#i11518 )
2 CONT
