1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was probably a sister of Gorloïs, and if so probably a daughter of Sartogys. Her husband, the historical Cador, king of Dumnonia, was probably the Cador who is said in Arthurian legend to have succeeded Gorlois
2 CONC  as duke of Cornwall. Her son Constantine is called a cousin of King Arthur, which suggests either Cador or his wife was a sibling of Gorloïs. If Cador was the historical king of Dumnonia then his ancestry is known, so the relatio
2 CONC nship to Gorloïs would have to be through Cador's wife. 
