2 CONT Source: Kraentzler 1770. K: Attila (Accia).   K. has problems with this line. He indicates either Caius Octavius (RIN 3507) or Appius Claudius Nero was the father of Tiberius Claudius Nero II--with Attila being married to whicheve
2 CONC r wins out, apparently.   Also, in line 1826 he leaves out this generation (chickened out apparently) and had Tiberius Claudius I the father of Tiberius Claudius II.   Duran has charts alleging "Atia Caesonia" married C. Octavius 
2 CONC Caesar and they were the parents of Octavius Augustus Caesar.
