2 CONT =Marcus Appuleius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Appuleius (c.55-c. 15 BC) was a Roman Senator who was appointed Roman consul in 20 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Appuleius is postulated to have been the son of Sextus Appuleius and Octavia the Elder, therefore making him related to the emperor Augustus through his grandfather Gaius Octavius. For many years associated with the quaesto
2 CONC r of Asia in 45 BC who joined Marcus Junius Brutus after the assassination of Julius Caesar, this is now held to have been his uncle of the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 23/22 BC, Marcus Appuleius was a legate at Tridentum. He was next elected Roman consul in 20 BC, while Augustus was away from Rome. Unlike the elections of 21 BC and 19 BC, these were not interrupted by electoral discord.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no record of him taking any other post after his consulship. It has therefore been speculated that Marcus Appuleius died sometime shortly after his consulship, and definitely by the time that Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa had 
2 CONC died in 12 BC, as Appuleius’ brother Sextus Appuleius the consul of 29 BC was present at the funeral, but Marcus was not.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Appuleius
