2 CONT =Marcus Lollius Paulinus Decimus Valerius Asiaticus Saturninus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Lollius Paulinus Decimus Valerius Asiaticus Saturninus (69/70-after 134) was a prominent Roman Senator who was a powerful figure in the second half of the 1st century and first half of the 2nd century.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family Background & Early Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus was of Allobrogian and Roman ancestry. He was the son of the Decimus Valerius Asiaticus from his wife Vitellia, the daughter of the Roman emperor Vitellius from his wife Galeria Fundana. His father served as a Legatus o
2 CONC f Gallia Belgica, he later became the Roman governor of that province in the reign of the Roman emperor Nero. The father of Saturninus, became powerful through wealth and the skilful exploitation of imperial patronage.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of his father were originally from Vienna, Gallia Narbonensis. Saturninus was a direct descendant of the consul, Roman Senator Decimus Valerius Asiaticus and his wife Lollia Saturnina, whose younger sister Lollia Paulin
2 CONC a was a Roman empress and the third wife of the Roman emperor Caligula. Saturninus was a grandson to Decimus Valerius Asiaticus and Lollia Saturnina. The name of Saturninus reveals paternally he is related to the gens, Valeria, Lo
2 CONC llia and gens, Volusia.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Vespasian became Roman emperor in second half of 69, Asiaticus was appointment for a consulship in 70. Before he could serve his consulship in early 70, Asiaticus died. Asiaticus was survived by Vitellia and their son. Later 
2 CONC in 70, Vespasian arranged Vitellia to remarry another unnamed groom. Her second marriage was a splendid match for her and Vespasian provided for her, the dowry and clothing. Although he was born in Vienna, he was raised in Rome. L
2 CONC ittle is known on early life.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Political career'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus started his political career in the reign of the Roman emperor Domitian who ruled from 81 til 96. He served as a Triumvir Monetalis; was a board member of the Salius collinus and the Pontiff. Between the years about 85 
2 CONC to 90 he served as a Quaestor and Praetor. Saturninus served as a suffect consul in 93 or in 94.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus served as a Proconsul of Asia in 108 to 109. From the years 124 til 134, he served as a Praefectus urbi in Rome. In 125, he served again as a consul. During his political career in the first half of the second century, 
2 CONC he was friends with the Roman emperors Trajan and Hadrian.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage and Issue'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturninus married as his wife, the noblewoman Valeria Catulla Messallina who came from a family of consular rank. Messallina bore Asiaticus a son called Decimus Valerius Taurus Catullus Messallinus Asiaticus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Lollius_Paulinus_Decimus_Valerius_Asiaticus_Saturninus
