0 @N6000000003051149743@ NOTE By 486, he had significantly increased the extent of Merovingian domains,as a result, many important cities, including Troyes, Reims and Amiens, were incorporated into the realm.
1 CONT He was baptised by Saint Remy on Christmas Eve, 496, and it was through him that the Church of Rome began to establish her undisputed supremacy which would remain unchallenged for over 1000 years. It is important to note that Clov
1 CONC is' baptism was NOT a coronation, as has been suggested. The Church did NOT make Clovis a king. He was already that and the Church could do was to recognize him as such. But virtue of doing such, the Church bound itself, not to Cl
1 CONC ovis alone, but to his sucessors as well, to the bloodline.
1 CONT (HB,HG)
