0 @N6000000001355550857@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT Emperor of Rome in the West 364-375
1 CONT During the reigns of the Emperors Julian (361-363) and Jovian (363-364), Valentinian was a major military figure. When Jovian died in 363, the Roman army raised him up as Emperor, and the decision was ratifiedby the Senate. Valent
1 CONC inian appointed his brother, Valens, to rule with him in the East. Valentinian himself took Illyricum, Italy, Gaul, Britain, Africa, and Spain under his direct administration, leaving theeastern provinces to his brother. Under Val
1 CONC entinian's rule, the Romanarmy won many battles in Africa and Britain, and in Germany against the Alamanni and the Saxons. Valentinian furthered education throught the Empire, provided medical care for the poor, and though he was 
1 CONC an orthodox Christian he tolerated all religions.
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------  ------
