0 @N6000000001353749886@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT Emperor of Rome in the West 375-392
1 CONT Valentinian II succeeded on the death of his father in 375, only 4 years old, to rule with his brother Gratian (Valentinian II was granted Africa, Italy, and part of Illyricum). During his minority, Justinia administered the gover
1 CONC nment. In 387, he was driven out of Italy by the Emperor Maximus who had deposed his brother and gained all of Gaul, Britain, and Spain. Valentinian sought protection with the Emperor Theodosius who administered the East, who rest
1 CONC ored him to power in 388 as sole-ruler of the West (Maximus was killed). Valentinian was murdered in 392 by his general Argobast who placed the puppet Eugenius on the throne.
