0 @N6000000002244390026@ NOTE Clovis was the Merovingian founder of the Frankish kingdom that dominated
1 CONT much of western Europe in the early Middle Ages. At Soissons, in 486, he
1 CONT defeated Syagrius, the last Roman ruler in Gaul. His family was secure in an
1 CONT unrivaled dominance that was to last until the 8th century.
0 @N6000000002248230376@ NOTE kinsman of Clovis I
0 @N6000000002906217926@ NOTE DESCENT:  Frederick Lewis Weis and Walter Lee Sheppard, Jr., Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700, (Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Co., 7th ed., 1992) at 163.  Line 190-1.
0 @N6000000003319677216@ NOTE
1 CONT !REIGNED: King of Franks (481 - 511) 
1 CONT King of France 
1 CONT Founder of the Empire of the Franks 
1 CONT
1 CONT c.466-511, Frankish king (481-511), founder of the MEROVINGIAN monarchy. He rose from tribal chief to sole leader of the Salian FRANKS by dint of patience and murder. He won Gaul and SW Germany by fighting the Romans, Alemanni, Bu
1 CONC rgundians, and Visigoths. His wife, St. Clotilda, encouraged his conversion (496) to Christianity. 
1 CONT
1 CONT FILE: Concise Columbia Electronic Encyclopedia Copyright 1994, Columbia University Press. 
1 CONT
1 CONT FILE: Peter Grard Gentala 
1 CONT
1 CONT REIGNED: King of Cologne 
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTE: kinsman of Clovis I "the Great", King of the Salic Franks 
1 CONT
1 CONT NAME: Clovis the Riparian, K. of Cologne, Flourished about 420.
