0 @N6000000002187576295@ NOTE wife of Rodobertus *620. Source: Dan Pomerleau 
0 @N6000000002176649986@ NOTE Ebroin, the mayor of the palace of Neustria from 656, took it upon himself to
1 CONT appoint Theodoric III as successor when Chlotar III died in 673. The magnates
1 CONT rebelled at the lack of consultation and called upon a 3rd brother, king
1 CONT Childeric II of Austrasia, but he was assassinated in 675. Ebroin escaped but
1 CONT implicated St. Leodegar, bishop of Autun. The bishop's tongue and lips were
1 CONT cut off before being finally executed. Ebroin's cruelty and oppression were
1 CONT such, however, that he was later assassinated by a Frankish nobleman.
0 @N6000000002187572095@ NOTE wife of Chrodobertus. According to Europaische Stammtafeln volume II page 10: Doda/Detta had possibly six children : Landrada who married Sigramus, unnamed daughter married to Lievin who became bishop of Trier and a saint, Grimber
1 CONC t, St.Rupert (Robert) Bishop of Worms, St.Galaberge. These children are possible, the one *certain* child, however, is Lambert II Lantbertus. Lambert II is also listed in Genealogisches Handbuch des Adels, Fuerstlichen Haueser 196
1 CONC 1, page 9. Source: Leo van de Pas. 
