0 @N6000000002187709177@ NOTE Sunno
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Sunno was a Frankish duke (dux, leader), or war chief, in the late 4th century. Gregory of Tours mentions him in his Historia Francorum, together with dukes Marcomer and Genobaud. They crossed the Rhine, raided the Roman province 
1 CONC of Germania and threatened Cologne, in the latter years of Western Roman Emperor Magnus Maximus (c. 388). They reportedly also led the Chatti and the Ampsivarii.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sunno was killed by his own men in 388 after winning a battle against the Romans.
