0 @N6000000002187580480@ NOTE Valens
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Flavius Julius Valens (Latin: IMP CAESAR FLAVIVS IVLIVS VALENS AVGVSTVS) (328 – August 9, 378) was Roman Emperor (364 - 378), after he was given the Eastern part of the empire by his brother Valentinian I. His father was the gener
1 CONC al Gratian the Elder. Valens was known as the Last True Roman.
1 CONT
