0 @N6000000002187718038@ NOTE Marcus Valerius Messalla Messallinus
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marcus Valerius Messalla Messallinus was the son of the famous orator Marcus Valerius Messalla Corvinus, whom he resembled in character. He was a senator and consul in 3 BC and AD 3. Messallinus suggested to Tiberius an oath of al
1 CONC legiance should be sworn to him yearly; he also suggested two golden statues be placed in two temples, in celebration of Rome's foreign victories and in memory of Germanicus, which Tiberius rejected. He married Caesar Augustus' ni
1 CONC ece Claudia Marcella Minor, her second husband. Their son Marcus Valerius Messalla Barbatus was the father of Claudius' wife Valeria Messalina.
0 @N6000000002187712733@ NOTE Marcus Valerius Messalla Barbatus
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Marcus Valerius Messala Barbatus Messalinus (12 BC - 20/21) was a consul of ancient Rome. He was the father of the Roman Empress Valeria Messalina.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was son to Marcus Valerius Messalla Messallinus and Claudia Marcella Minor. His father served twice as consul. His paternal grandfather was the famous orator Marcus Valerius Messala Corvinus. His maternal grandparents were Gaiu
1 CONC s Claudius Marcellus and Octavia Minor, sister of Augustus.
1 CONT
1 CONT Messala Barbatus had married his half first-cousin Domitia Lepida at an unknown date. Their marriage resulted with a son Marcus Valerius Messala Corvinus, who became consul in 58, and Valeria Messalina (20-48).
1 CONT
1 CONT Messala Barbatus became consul in 20. Little is known of his life. One theory of modern historians is that he died of an early death in 20 or early 21. His only sibling was his elder half-sister Claudia Pulchra who had married the
1 CONC  Roman general and politician Publius Quinctilius Varus.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Marcus Junius Silanus Torquatus and Lucius Norbanus Balbus Consul of the Roman Empire together with Marcus Aurelius Cotta Maximus Messalinus
1 CONT 20 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Tiberius and Julius Caesar Drusus 
