1 CONC ship; that men ought now to be more circumspect in addressing him, and to regard his word as law. So far did he go in his presumption, that when a soothsayer once reported direful inwards without a heart, he said: "They will be mo
1 CONC re favourable when I wish it; it should not be regarded as a portent, if a beast has no heart..." 
