0 @N6000000002187712526@ NOTE Octavia Minor
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Octavia Minor (69 - 11 BC), also known as Octavia the Younger or simply Octavia, was the sister of the first Roman Emperor, Augustus, and half sister of Octavia Thurina Major. She was one of the most prominent women in Roman histo
1 CONC ry[citation needed], respected and admired by contemporaries for her loyalty, nobility and humanity and for maintaining traditional Roman feminine virtues. Octavia lived at a time when many succumbed to treachery and intrigue.
1 CONT
